eSpeak NG
---------

The extension bundles eSpeak NG as compiled JavaScript inside
libs/kokoro/kokoro.web.js. That compiled form is not source.

  Upstream source:   https://github.com/espeak-ng/espeak-ng
  Compiled form came from:  the npm package phonemizer version 1.2.1,
                            https://www.npmjs.com/package/phonemizer
                            which ships it as src/espeakng.worker.js and
                            data/espeakng.worker.data

The exact upstream revision that this compiled build was produced from is NOT
currently identified. The bundle carries no version string for eSpeak NG, and
phonemizer 1.2.1 does not record which revision it built from. This notice does
not claim otherwise, and no particular upstream commit should be inferred from
it.

The intended fix is to rebuild the engine from a pinned, recorded eSpeak NG
revision and to state that revision here, so that the corresponding source for
the compiled form can be identified exactly. That work is planned and is not
part of this release. Anyone who needs the corresponding source for the
compiled eSpeak NG as currently shipped should treat phonemizer 1.2.1 as the
immediate upstream and raise the revision question there; the relevant issue is
xenova/phonemizer.js#6, which is open and unanswered.

